# Shop Java Guidance

For production Java, read and follow `.github/instructions/core-java.instructions.md`.
For Java tests, also read and follow `.github/instructions/core-tests.instructions.md`.
Do not duplicate those scoped rules here; update their canonical source when project-specific guidance changes.

## Shop-Specific Java Rules

- Use Adventure `Component` for all user-facing text (no Bungee chat)
- Use Folia-safe scheduling for world, block, sign, and region-sensitive operations
- Use thread-safe collections for mutable data shared between scheduler contexts
- Keep optional integrations optional; detect plugins at runtime
- Preserve legacy `&` formatting only where it remains an intentional compatibility feature
- Treat placeholder substitutions as plain text, not MiniMessage input
- Do not reintroduce `org.spigotmc.*` imports or NMS modules
